# Main and nightly stay together

When the user asks to put work on **main** (`메인에 올려`, push/merge to `origin/main`):

1. Fast-forward `main` to the release commit and `git push origin main`.
2. **Also** fast-forward `nightly` to that same commit and `git push origin nightly`.
3. Do not leave `origin/nightly` behind `origin/main`.

Do not force-push either branch. If they are not a fast-forward, stop and say so.

This is only for an explicit “put it on main” request. A version-bump commit stays local until they ask.
